  "finding": "The DOI resolver returned the most complete record of all — authors, year, journal, volume, pages and ISSN — in 0.4 s, from a publisher page that refuses direct access. Where a DOI is known, resolving it beats visiting the article page.",
  "limits": [
    "Three publishers (MDPI, ScienceDirect, DOAJ) answer 403 to any server-side reader. That is their policy, not a defect here, and the browser extension reaches them.",
    "Pages and ISSN are missing where the platform does not declare them — PubMed omits page numbers on the abstract page. Nothing is filled in from elsewhere.",
    "18 platforms is a survey of the common ones, not a census."
